the creators are the values reaching fresh_uid, transitively: true
the derivation of the stand-in refuses nothing: true
a tnode.ml with no top-level fresh_uid is refused: true
a local fresh_uid shadowing the top-level one mints nothing: true
a uid minted inside a nested module is refused, not ignored: true
a creation bound and noted is accepted: true
a creation bound and never noted is refused: true
a pair-returning creator bound by a tuple pattern and noted is accepted: true
a creation flowing through match arms into a noted variable is accepted, every arm: true
the same flow with no note refuses both creations: true
noting a different variable of the same name does not count: true
a creation bound to no variable is refused: true
a creation in argument position is refused as unfollowed: true
a creation returned from a function body is refused as unfollowed: true
a creator referenced without being applied is refused: true
a call of a value that mints no uid is not a creation: true
a shadowing local note_open_node is not the real one: true
outside tensor.ml, a top-level note_open_node is not the real one: true
a note_open_node defined in a nested module is not the real one: true
a second top-level note_open_node is refused: true
Ir.Tnode.create, spelled out, is a creation: true
Tnode.create after open Ir is a creation: true
a bare create under a local open of Tn is a creation: true
the same under the open, noted, is accepted: true
a name the open of Tn brings in shadows a local binding of it: true
a locally bound module Tn is not Ir.Tnode: true
a locally bound module Ir is not the library: true
a source that does not parse is the input's fault, not the scanner's: true
